      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s first county seat was Webster, but in the 1880s Sylva took over because the railroad and a booming economy made it more central.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.discoverjacksonnc.com/your-trip/history-heritage/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Whitewater Falls, a 411‑foot drop, sits in Jackson County and ranks among the highest waterfalls east of the Rockies.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
